  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345162",
      "title": "Why Do You Need A Special Project Setup?",
      "sourceHash": "dd1e682b30db7ab6eb465bef8e8e7cadfffa4d71498bddd4b8b5f4ab01781639",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 1.74,
          "en": "So why do we need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.74,
          "end": 4.41,
          "en": "such a CodeSandbox environment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.41,
          "end": 9.41,
          "en": "or such a local project created with extra tools like Vite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 13.47,
          "en": "if we simply wanna write some React code?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.47,
          "end": 18.47,
          "en": "Why can't we just create an HTML file and a JavaScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.47,
          "end": 23.73,
          "en": "and reference the script file from inside the HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.73,
          "end": 27.66,
          "en": "and then put our React code into that script file?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.66,
          "end": 30.633,
          "en": "Why is that not really an option?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.68,
          "end": 33.29,
          "en": "Well, it isn't really an option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.29,
          "end": 36.6,
          "en": "because when writing React code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.6,
          "end": 41.6,
          "en": "you'll use this special HTML in JavaScript feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.97,
          "end": 46.74,
          "en": "which I already showed you earlier in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.74,
          "end": 49.5,
          "en": "This syntax is called JSX,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.5,
          "end": 52.89,
          "en": "and you will learn more about it throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.89,
          "end": 54.86,
          "en": "But what's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.86,
          "end": 57.25,
          "en": "about this special syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.25,
          "end": 61.124,
          "en": "which you will use all the time in React projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.124,
          "end": 65.01,
          "en": "is that it unfortunately doesn't work in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.01,
          "end": 68.43,
          "en": "which of course is a rather big problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.43,
          "end": 73.08,
          "en": "So therefore the code you write actually must be transformed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.08,
          "end": 75.99,
          "en": "to code that does run in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.99,
          "end": 80.223,
          "en": "Also, because you typically want to optimize this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 80.223,
          "end": 81.93,
          "en": "and for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.93,
          "end": 84.57,
          "en": "shorten variable and function names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.57,
          "end": 86.756,
          "en": "and remove excess white space",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.756,
          "end": 90.26,
          "en": "so that the code that has to be downloaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.26,
          "end": 95.25999999999999,
          "en": "by your website visitors is as small as possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.67,
          "end": 98.88,
          "en": "to improve the performance of your website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.88,
          "end": 103.068,
          "en": "And that's the reason why you need to create React projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.068,
          "end": 106.05,
          "en": "with extra tools like Vite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.05,
          "end": 107.78999999999999,
          "en": "because it's then, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.78999999999999,
          "end": 111.542,
          "en": "those tools which do transform your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.542,
          "end": 116.542,
          "en": "to code that can be executed efficiently in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.72999999999999,
          "end": 118.625,
          "en": "That's why you can't just create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 118.625,
          "end": 121.71,
          "en": "a basic HTML and script file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.71,
          "end": 125.88,
          "en": "but why you instead do need those extra tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 125.88,
          "end": 129.36,
          "en": "But fortunately, as you saw in the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.36,
          "end": 131.88,
          "en": "creating projects with those tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.88,
          "end": 133.98,
          "en": "is pretty straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.98,
          "end": 137.164,
          "en": "Of course, especially if you use the CodeSandbox environment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.164,
          "end": 141.72,
          "en": "because you there basically don't have to do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.72,
          "end": 144.211,
          "en": "And as mentioned in the last lecture as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.211,
          "end": 147.469,
          "en": "throughout this course, in all those course sections,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.469,
          "end": 151.02,
          "en": "I will always give you starting projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.02,
          "end": 154.77,
          "en": "both a CodeSandbox and a local version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.77,
          "end": 157.32,
          "en": "so that you actually don't have to create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.32,
          "end": 159.27,
          "en": "any projects at all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.27,
          "end": 162.652,
          "en": "but you can instead use those starting projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.652,
          "end": 166.56,
          "en": "and work in those so that you can really focus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.56,
          "end": 169.263,
          "en": "on learning and writing React code.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
